<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Find a map</title>
<meta name="dcterms.created" content="{{ timestamp }}"><meta name="dcterms.modified" content="{{ timestamp }}">
<style>
@font-face{font-family:MapFinder;src:url("{{ font_uri }}")}
@page{size:90mm 160mm;margin:9mm 8mm 15mm;@bottom-center{content:"Draft navigation · " counter(page) "\A Traducción automática sin revisar.";white-space:pre;font-size:8pt;color:#666}}
body{font-family:MapFinder;font-size:12pt;line-height:1.35;color:#172536}
h1{font-size:20pt;line-height:1.15}h2{font-size:15pt;break-after:avoid}p{margin:0 0 10pt;break-inside:avoid}
li{margin-bottom:8pt;break-inside:avoid}.path{overflow-wrap:anywhere}.notes{font-size:8pt;color:#666}
</style></head><body>
<h1>Find a map</h1>
<ol><li>Open your state’s folder.</li><li>Open your county’s folder.</li><li>If you see <b>0_OVERVIEW.pdf</b>, open it to find ZIP areas.</li><li>Open the detailed map. Pinch to zoom, and move around the page.</li></ol>
<p>The PDF maps open directly. The <b>android</b> folder holds optional map data for a separate app.</p>
<p lang="es">Abra la carpeta de su estado y luego la de su condado. Si ve <b>0_OVERVIEW.pdf</b>, ábralo para encontrar las áreas de códigos postales. Amplíe el mapa detallado con los dedos.</p>
<p>Some county folders have only an area sample so far. Check the area named in the file.</p>
<p class="notes">Spanish navigation text is an unreviewed machine translation. These are the map and places PDFs actually present in this incomplete preview. Use the folder paths below; local links vary between phone viewers.</p>
{% for (state, county), files in groups.items() %}
<h2>{{ state }} / {{ county }}</h2><p class="path">3_MAPS_AND_PLACES/{{ state }}/{{ county }}/</p>
<ul>{% for file in files %}<li class="path">{{ file.name }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
{% endfor %}
</body></html>
